1. Create Topic

sh kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --create --topic perf-test --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1

2. Producer Performance Test

Send 100,000 messages, each 1 KB.

sh kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic perf-test --num-records 100000 --record-size 1024 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092

======================================
Parameter	            Meaning
num-records	        Number of messages
record-size	        Message size in bytes
throughput -1	      Maximum speed
bootstrap.servers	  Kafka broker
======================================

3. Producer with Acks=all

sh kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic perf-test --num-records 100000 --record-size 1024 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 acks=all

================================
acks=0     Fastest
acks=1     Balanced
acks=all   Safest but slower
================================

4. Producer Compression Test

sh kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic perf-test --num-records 100000 --record-size 1024 --throughput -1 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 compression.type=snappy

================
No Compression
Snappy
LZ4
ZSTD
===============

5. Consumer Performance Test

Consume from beginning.

sh kafka-consumer-perf-test.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic perf-test --messages 100000 


6. Multi-Partition Test

Create topic:

sh kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --create --topic perf-test-12 --partitions 12 --replication-factor 1

=================================
3 partitions  -> Lower throughput

12 partitions -> Higher throughput
==================================

7. Demonstrate Batching Impact

Small batch:

sh kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic perf-test --num-records 100000 --record-size 100 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 batch.size=16384

Large batch:

sh kafka-producer-perf-test.sh --topic perf-test --num-records 100000 --record-size 100 --producer-props bootstrap.servers=localhost:9092 batch.size=65536

====================
Larger batches
      ↓
Fewer network calls
      ↓
Higher throughput
====================


Question & Answers
===================

>> Why is producer slower with acks=all?

Leader writes
     ↓
Followers replicate
     ↓
Acknowledgment sent

More durability, slightly lower throughput.

>> Why do more partitions increase throughput?

Kafka can write in parallel.

